# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build trees. Each is a full CMake configuration that regenerates from
# CMakeLists.txt, so none of it belongs in the repo:
#   build/      the normal Release tree (build.sh writes here)
#   build_asan/ an AddressSanitizer tree, configured by hand with
#               -fsanitize=address -fno-omit-frame-pointer -g -O0, used to
#               catch out-of-bounds writes. Not referenced by build.sh.
# The catch-all matches any other build* tree (build_debug, etc.) too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build*/

# Compiled executables. Kept as an empty directory so build.sh has somewhere
# to write without mkdir'ing first.
bin/*
!bin/.gitkeep

# Slurm job output collected here by the sbatch scripts.
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep

# Slurm writes these wherever a job happens to run, not just under logs/.
*.out
*.err

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project directories. A project holds one simulation's inputs and its
# outputs; only the hand-written inputs are worth tracking. Example_Project
# doubles as the template a new project gets copied from, so its config and
# run scripts DO belong in the repo -- everything a run generates does not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Projects/*/output/*
!Projects/*/output/.gitkeep

# plots/ and sherlock_log/ are NOT listed here on purpose. Each owns a local
# .gitignore that ignores its own contents but keeps itself, so the directory
# survives a fresh clone (the plotting script and sbatch both need it to
# already exist). Excluding those directories from here instead would stop git
# descending into them, and the local .gitignore would never be read.

# Any project other than the Example_Project template is somebody's actual
# simulation -- local scratch, not shared code.
Projects/*
!Projects/README.md
!Projects/Example_Project/

# Byte-identical duplicates of Projects/Example_Project/coordinates.json and
# A_0.2.json. Left out until it's decided which location owns the grid
# geometry, rather than committing two copies that can drift apart.
data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / tooling droppings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Compiled objects and libraries, in case anything is ever built in-tree
# rather than in build/.
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*

*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
